Test compile_flags are passed to JS file emission

  $ make_melange_project 3.13 0.1

  $ cat > main.ml <<EOF
  > let () = Js.log "hello"
  > EOF

  $ cat > dune <<EOF
  > (melange.emit
  >  (target output)
  >  (emit_stdlib false)
  >  (modules main)
  >  (compile_flags :standard --mel-no-version-header))
  > EOF

  $ dune build @melange

File is generated with the "Generated by Melange" header even though we
specified the opposite in flags

  $ cat _build/default/output/main.js
  'use strict';
  
  
  console.log("hello");
  /*  Not a pure module */

Flags may be generated by a rule inside the emit target directory. Including
them must produce the same output as specifying them directly above.

  $ mkdir generated-flags
  $ cd generated-flags
  $ make_melange_project 3.13 0.1
  $ cp ../main.ml .
  $ cat > dune <<EOF
  > (melange.emit
  >  (target out)
  >  (emit_stdlib false)
  >  (compile_flags :standard (:include out/flags.sexp)))
  > EOF
  $ mkdir out
  $ cat > out/dune <<EOF
  > (rule
  >  (target flags.sexp)
  >  (action (write-file %{target} "(--mel-no-version-header)")))
  > EOF
  $ dune build out/main.js
  $ cmp ../_build/default/output/main.js _build/default/out/main.js
